{"segs": ["PA_ja_95:0.2", "PA_ja_95:0.3"], "en": "The First Collection (Ekakanipāta), Chapter on the Leaf (Littavagga)", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_95:0.4"], "en": "5. The Mahāsudassana Jātaka:", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_95:1.1", "PA_ja_95:1.2"], "en": "“Impermanent indeed are conditioned things, subject to arising and passing away;”", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_95:1.3"], "en": "Having arisen, they cease;", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_95:1.4"], "en": "their subsiding is blissful.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_95:2.1"], "en": "Thus ends the Mahāsudassana Jātaka, the fifth.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"}
